Replaces: fonts-patrone-sans (<< 2.0.0)
Description: PatroneOS's fonts: Sans, Mono, Document, Serif and Classic
 PatroneOS's own five font families, drawn from scratch: PatroneOS Sans, the
 desktop's font; PatroneOS Mono, the terminal's, one width throughout, with
 box-drawing characters; PatroneOS Document, for documents; PatroneOS Serif;
 and PatroneOS Classic, a plain sans. Each has a tailed l, so I, l, 1 and |
 all differ, and no slashed zero.
 .
 PatroneOS Document and PatroneOS Classic give each letter the width of the
 fonts documents most often ask for (patrone-branding's fontconfig sends
 Calibri to Document, and Arial and Helvetica to Classic), so those documents
 keep their layout. Noto Sans covers the scripts the fonts don't; Liberation
 Serif and Caladea stand in for the classic serif fonts.
